">As of Oct 12, the record for Cabell County runs from 1951 to 2025, 75 years on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids. September to October, October to November and February to March each came in under 90% of normal in 34 of those years. In 2026 so far, January to February and February to March both sat at 63% of normal on the middle of the grids. Every grid had its driest year in 1963, with grid 21791 at 71%.</p>"}
